n        "clustering_by_layer": {\n          "value": "global_clustering_family, global_clustering_work_school, global_clustering_community",\n          "source": "social_network.json",\n          "confidence": "Medium",\n          "notes": "Compute on undirected version; match approximately in synthetic rewiring."\n        },\n        "mixing_matrices": {\n          "value": "P(contact | age_group_i \\u2192 age_group_j) and P(contact | occupation_i \\u2192 occupation_j) per layer",\n          "source": "social_network.json joined with agent_attributes.csv",\n          "confidence": "Medium",\n          "notes": "Estimate empirical mixing; enforce during edge wiring in synthetic networks."\n        },\n        "layer_influence_weights": {\n          "value": {\n            "family": 1.0,\n            "work_school": 0.6,\n            "community": 0.3\n          },\n          "source": "Expert prior; to be calibrated against train_data adoption dynamics",\n          "confidence": "Low",\n          "notes": "Relative weights in aggregating neighbor influence; calibrate to match adoption responsiveness across layers if layer exposures can be inferred."\n        },\n        "interaction_rates_per_layer_per_day": {\n          "value": {\n            "family": 0.8,\n            "work_school": 1.5,\n            "community": 1.0\n          },\n          "source": "Expert prior; adjust to match contact frequency assumptions",\n          "confidence": "Low",\n          "notes": "Expected number of salient interactions per agent per day by layer; scales the amount of social exposure."\n        }\n      },\n      "behavior_dynamics": {\n        "initial_mask_prevalence": {\n          "value": "p_init_mask = mean(agent_attributes.initial_mask_wearing) or prevalence at day=min(train_data.day)",\n          "source": "agent_attributes.csv and/or train_data.csv",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Use agent_attributes for seeding unless time series provides an earlier baseline."\n        },\n        "p_adopt_no_info": {\n          "value": "P(Mt=1 | Mt-1=0, received_info_t=0)",\n          "source": "train_data.csv",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Compute from transitions; serves as baseline adoption absent info and peer effects."\n        },\n        "p_adopt_with_info": {\n          "value": "P(Mt=1 | Mt-1=0, received_info_t=1)",\n          "source": "train_data.csv",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Captures incremental effect of info on same day (can also include received_info_{t-1})."\n        },\n        "p_drop": {\n          "value": "P(Mt=0 | Mt-1=1)",\n          "source": "train_data.csv",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Controls adherence decay; can be modeled as constant or dependent on info/peers."\n        },\n        "peer_influence_coefficient": {\n          "value": "\\u03b2_peer (log-odds increase per unit weighted neighbor_mask_share)",\n          "source": "Calibrate using train_data with simulated exposure or using social_network.json + observed neighbor states if available",\n          "confidence": "Medium",\n          "notes": "Use logistic model: logit(P(adopt)) = \\u03b20 + \\u03b2_info*info + \\u03b2_peer*E_t + \\u03b2_risk*risk + interactions; E_t = \\u03a3_L w_L * masked_share_L."\n        },\n        "risk_susceptibility_scaler": {\n          "value": 1.0,\n          "source": "Expert prior; refine to fit",\n          "confidence": "Low",\n          "notes": "Maps risk_perception into threshold/susceptibility: \\u03b8_i = \\u03b80 - \\u03b1*risk_i; start \\u03b1=1.0."\n        },\n        "exogenous_noise_flip": {\n          "value": 0.005,\n          "source": "Expert prior",\n          "confidence": "Low",\n          "notes": "Small probability of random state change to account for unobserved shocks."\n        }\n      },\n      "information_dynamics": {\n        "external_info_rate": {\n          "value": "lambda_info = mean(received_info_t)",\n          "source": "train_data.csv",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "If modeling info as diffusion, treat this as baseline exogenous rate."\n        },\n        "peer_info_transmission_prob_per_contact": {\n          "value": {\n            "family": "\\u03c4_family",\n            "work_school": "\\u03c4_work_school",\n            "community": "\\u03c4_community"\n          },\n          "source": "Calibrate so simulated received_info prevalence and clustering match train_data",\n          "confidence": "Medium",\n          "notes": "Use multiplex independent cascade for info spread; constrain \\u03c4_family \\u2265 \\u03c4_work_school \\u2265 \\u03c4_community."\n        },\n        "info_effect_size_on_adoption": {\n          "value": "\\u03b2_info = log(OR_info) where OR_info = p_on_info*(1-p_on_noinfo) / [(1-p_on_info)*p_on_noinfo]",\n          "source": "Derived from train_data.csv transitions",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Plug into adoption logistic model; can allow lagged effects \\u03b2_info_lag."\n        },\n        "info_memory_decay_days": {\n          "value": 1,\n          "source": "Assumption based on train_data definition (daily flag)",\n          "confidence": "Medium",\n          "notes": "If evidence of lagged effects, extend to 2\\u20133 days with decay."\n        }\n      },\n      "scheduler_and_timing": {\n        "time_step_days": {\n          "value": 1,\n          "source": "train_data.csv (daily time index)",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Synchronous daily updates."\n        },\n        "warmup_days": {\n          "value": 0,\n          "source": "Design choice",\n          "confidence": "Low",\n          "notes": "Set >0 if initializing from agent_attributes but validating against later train_data window."\n        },\n        "simulation_horizon_days": {\n          "value": "match max(train_data.day) - min(train_data.day) + 1",\n          "source": "train_data.csv",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Extend for forecasting scenarios."\n        }\n      },\n      "observation_and_validation": {\n        "observed_variables": {\n          "value": [\n            "wearing_mask (state)",\n            "received_info (event)"\n          ],\n          "source": "train_data.csv",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Assumed measured without error; if not, add observation noise."\n        },\n        "target_moments": {\n          "value": [\n            "daily prevalence",\n            "transition rates",\n            "duration distributions",\n            "agent-level adoption curves"\n          ],\n          "source": "train_data.csv",\n          "confidence": "High",\n          "notes": "Use as calibration and validation targets."\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "calibration_strategy": {\n      "preprocessing_steps": [\n        {\n          "step": "Align agent_id across files and restrict to intersection set",\n          "purpose": "Ensure consistent population across attributes, network, and time series."\n        },\n        {\n          "step": "Validate total_connections consistency",\n          "purpose": "Check agent_attributes total_connections equals sum of layer-specific degrees; flag anomalies."\n        },\n        {\n          "step": "Network sanitation and symmetrization decision",\n          "purpose": "Compute reciprocity; choose directed influence or symmetrize adjacency; construct undirected edges if required."\n        },\n        {\n          "step": "Compute per-layer degrees, clustering, and mixing matrices",\n          "purpose": "Summarize topology for configuration and synthetic network generation if needed."\n        },\n        {\n          "step": "Construct per-agent daily lag features",\n          "purpose": "From train_data, create mask_{t-1}, received_info_t, received_info_{t-1}, and transition indicators."\n        },\n        {\n          "step": "Estimate baseline transition probabilities",\n          "purpose": "Compute p_on_noinfo, p_on_info, p_off and duration distributions as initial calibration targets."\n        },\n        {\n          "step": "Join risk_perception and demographics to time series",\n          "purpose": "Enable heterogeneous effect estimation and stratified validation."\n        }\n      ],\n      "calibration_approach": "Use a staged (hybrid frequentist + simulation-based) approach: (1) Estimate direct-from-data parameters: initial_mask_prevalence, p_on_noinfo, p_on_info, p_off, lambda_info, Beta(a,b) for risk_perception, degree/mixing summaries. (2) Fit a logistic model on train_data: logit(P(Mt=1)) = \\u03b20 + \\u03b3*Mt-1 + \\u03b2_info*received_info_t + \\u03b2_risk*risk_i + \\u03b2_demo*X_i. This yields \\u03b2_info, persistence \\u03b3, and baseline. (3) In the agent-based simulation, incorporate network exposure E_i,t = \\u03a3_L w_L * masked_share among neighbors per layer and add \\u03b2_peer for peer effects. Calibrate \\u03b2_peer, layer weights w_L, and peer info transmission \\u03c4_L via simulation-based optimization (e.g., ABC-SMC or Bayesian optimization) to match observed prevalence trajectory, transition rates, and (if available) spatial/network clustering of adoption. (4) If modeling info diffusion endogenously, match simulated received_info rates and their temporal autocorrelation to train_data. Prioritize identifiability by fixing either \\u03b2_peer or \\u03c4_L initially, then release both.",\n      "validation_strategy": "Hold out a time window (e.g., last 20% of days) and validate: (a) Aggregate prevalence: RMSE/MAE between simulated and observed daily mask prevalence. (b) Transition rates: compare p_on and p_off by day and by strata (age_group, occupation, degree quintiles). (c) Micro-level trajectories: Hamming distance or dynamic Brier score for agent-level mask states. (d) Network patterns: if neighbor states over time are available or reconstructable, validate clustering (Moran\\u2019s I) and community-level prevalence. Perform k-fold time-slice cross-validation and sensitivity analysis over key parameters (\\u03b2_peer, w_L, \\u03c4_L).",\n      "key_variables_to_calibrate": [\n        "\\u03b2_peer (peer influence strength)",\n        "w_L per layer (influence weights family/work_school/community)",\n        "\\u03c4_L per layer (info transmission probabilities)",\n        "\\u03b1 (risk_susceptibility_scaler)",\n        "interaction_rates_per_layer",\n        "exogenous_noise_flip"\n      ]\n    },\n    "file_summaries": [\n      {\n        "file_name": "agent_attributes.csv",\n        "file_type": "csv",\n        "semantic_summary": "- Overall data structure and type:\\n  - Flat CSV table; one row per agent.\\n  - Primary key: agent_id (integer, unique).\\n  - Columns/types:\\n    - age (int), age_group (categorical string), occupation (categorical string)\\n    - risk_perception (float 0\\u20131)\\n    - initial_mask_wearing (boolean)\\n    - family_connections, work_school_connections, community_connections, total_connections (integers)\\n  - total_connections equals the sum of the three layer-specific connection counts.\\n\\n- Relationships or nested elements:\\n  - No nested records or explicit edge lists; relationships are implicit via degree counts per social layer.\\n  - Implies a multiplex network with three layers: family, work/school, community. Each agent has a target degree in each layer.\\n  - Occupation and age_group suggest mixing constraints within layers (e.g., students in school layer; workers in work layer), but this is not explicitly encoded\\u2014must be inferred during network construction.\\n\\n- How this data should inform simulation entities or interactions:\\n  - Agent initialization:\\n    - Create one agent per row with attributes: age/age_group, occupation, risk_perception, initial_mask_wearing.\\n    - initial_mask_wearing sets the agent\\u2019s starting behavior state.\\n    - risk_perception provides a baseline propensity or threshold for adopting mask-wearing.\\n  - Network generation:\\n    - Construct three layer-specific networks matching each agent\\u2019s degree targets (family, work/school, community); total degree emerges from multiplex union.\\n    - Apply optional homophily/mixing rules using age_group and occupation to wire edges plausibly (e.g., students with students in school, workers with workers in work).\\n  - Interaction dynamics:\\n    - Social influence on mask adoption should be computed per layer, allowing different influence strengths (e.g., family > work/school > community) and aggregated to update behavior.\\n    - Age_group and occupation can modulate influence weights or contact frequency; risk_perception modulates susceptibility to peer influence.\\n  - Data checks/notes:\\n    - Validate total_connections consistency; handle any anomalies (e.g., young ages with work connections) per modeling assumptions rather than strict real-world constraints."\n      },\n      {\n        "file_name": "social_network.json",\n        "file_type": "json",\n        "semantic_summary": "- Overall data structure and type\\n  - JSON object mapping agent IDs (as strings) to adjacency lists (arrays of integers).\\n  - Each agent record contains four arrays: family, work_school, community, and all.\\n  - Topology is static (no timestamps); IDs appear to range 0\\u2013999.\\n\\n- Relationships or nested elements\\n  - family, work_school, community represent distinct network layers (tie contexts).\\n  - all is the deduplicated union of contacts across the three layers for that agent.\\n  - Edges are listed from the focal agent to others; reciprocity is not guaranteed (i.e., directed adjacency lists). Convert to undirected if needed by symmetrizing.\\n  - Layer sizes suggest stronger, smaller family networks; moderate work/school; larger community ties.\\n\\n- How this data should inform simulation entities or interactions\\n  - Age