eer effects are implicit and must be modeled or inferred externally.\\n  - Enables derivation of transition events (e.g., adopt, cease) via lagged states per agent.\\n\\n- How this data should inform simulation entities or interactions:\\n  - Entities: One agent per agent_id with state variables:\\n    - mask_state \\u2208 {true, false}\\n    - info_state \\u2208 {true, false} (possibly transient/per-day)\\n  - Time step: daily scheduler aligned with day.\\n  - Calibration targets:\\n    - Baseline transition probabilities P(mask_t | mask_{t-1}) to capture inertia/relapse.\\n    - Incremental effect of information P(mask_t | mask_{t-1}, received_info_t or received_info_{t-1}).\\n    - Durations of adherence and rates of switching absent info (spontaneous adoption/cessation).\\n  - Interactions:\\n    - Use received_info events as exogenous inputs or as outcomes of network diffusion; calibrate info-spread parameters (e.g., per-edge transmission) so simulated received_info rates match observed frequencies.\\n    - Initialize agents\\u2019 day 0 states from data when available; validate simulated trajectories against per-agent adoption curves and aggregate prevalence over time.\\n  - Missing elements to be supplied by the simulation:\\n    - Network topology (e.g., ER/WS/BA) and peer influence rules.\\n    - Any heterogeneity beyond agent_id (no demographics provided)."\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  "schemas": {\n    "agent_attributes.csv": {\n      "file_type": "csv",\n      "row_count": 1000,\n      "column_count": 10,\n      "columns": [\n        "agent_id",\n        "age",\n        "age_group",\n        "occupation",\n        "risk_perception",\n        "initial_mask_wearing",\n        "family_connections",\n        "work_school_connections",\n        "community_connections",\n        "total_connections"\n      ],\n      "data_info": "<class \'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame\'>\\nRangeIndex: 1000 entries, 0 to 999\\nData columns (total 10 columns):\\n #   Column            