 layer), but this is not explicitly encoded\\u2014must be inferred during network construction.\\n\\n- How this data should inform simulation entities or interactions:\\n  - Agent initialization:\\n    - Create one agent per row with attributes: age/age_group, occupation, risk_perception, initial_mask_wearing.\\n    - initial_mask_wearing sets the agent\\u2019s starting behavior state.\\n    - risk_perception provides a baseline propensity or threshold for adopting mask-wearing.\\n  - Network generation:\\n    - Construct three layer-specific networks matching each agent\\u2019s degree targets (family, work/school, community); total degree emerges from multiplex union.\\n    - Apply optional homophily/mixing rules using age_group and occupation to wire edges plausibly (e.g., students with students in school, workers with workers in work).\\n  - Interaction dynamics:\\n    - Social influence on mask adoption should be computed per layer, allowing different influence strengths (e.g., family > work/school > community) and aggregated to update behavior.\\n    - Age_group and occupation can modulate influence weights or contact frequency; risk_perception modulates susceptibility to peer influence.\\n  - Data checks/notes:\\n    - Validate total_connections consistency; handle any anomalies (e.g., young ages with work connections) per modeling assumptions rather than strict real-world constraints."\n    },\n    "social_network.json": {\n      "file_type": "json",\n      "data_type": "object",\n      "length": 1000,\n      "sample_data": {\n        "0": {\n          "family": [\n            80,\n            500,\n            122\n          ],\n          "work_school": [\n            1,\n            998,\n            5,\n            994\n          ],\n          "community": [\n            879,\n            712,\n            900,\n            533,\n            624,\n            691,\n            69,\n            315,\n            379,\n            647,\n            847\n    